+## Test Suite Reporting (devflow)
+
+Before claiming a slice, ticket or feature is done:
+
+1. **Run the full suite**, not only the tests you touched.
+2. **Name every failure**: the test identifier and a one-line reason. Never "a few failures" or "mostly passing".
+3. **Compare with the baseline** recorded when the worktree was created (devflow: `baseline` in `<main checkout>/.devflow/runs/iss-<N>.json`). Classify each failure:
+   - **New:** fails now, passed at baseline. Blocks completion.
+   - **Pre-existing:** failed at baseline too. Report it; it doesn't block, unless the task touched it.
+   - **Flaky:** re-run each failure once on its own; a test that passes on re-run is flagged flaky, never silently ignored.
+4. Also report **fixed** tests: failed at baseline, pass now.
+
+Report format:
+
+```
+Full suite: <command> → <P> passed, <F> failed (<N> new, <E> pre-existing, <K> flaky), <X> fixed vs baseline
+New failures:   <test id> — <reason>
+Pre-existing:   <test id>
+Flaky:          <test id>
+```
